{title: More Than an Ox}
{subtitle: Psalms 69:31}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Eb/G] | [Bb] [F/A] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I am [F/A]afflicted and in pain
[Gm]Let [Eb]your salvation lift me [Bb]high
Out of the [F/A]dust and out [Gm]of shame
[Eb]I see your light in the [F]sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will [Bb]praise the [F/A]name of [Gm]God with song
I will [Eb]magnify him [F]with thanksgiving
This will [Bb]please the [F/A]LORD more [Gm]than an ox
More than a [Eb]bull with [F]horns and [Bb]hooves [Ebmaj7][Eb6][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]You who seek [F/A]God let [Gm7]your hearts revive
[Eb]The humble will see it and be [Bb]glad
For the LORD hears the [F/A]needy [Gm]cry
[Eb]He does not despise his own [F]in chains
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will [Bb]praise the [F/A]name of [Gm]God with song
I will [Eb]magnify him [F]with thanksgiving
This [Bb]will please the [F/A]LORD more [Gm]than an ox
More than a [Eb]bull with [F]horns and [Bb]hooves
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I will praise the [F/A]name of God [Gm]with song [Eb][F][Bb]
This will please the [F/A]LORD more [Gm]than an ox [Eb][F][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
